      "listTimestamp": "Dec 5, 2025",
      "previewSnippet": "InMail Lola: Hi Richard, I’m reaching out about Thomas, a full-stack Data Scientist and ML Engineer with a BSc in Physics & Computer Science from University of Bristol and excellent commercial experience designing, deploying, and scaling production-grade machine learning and data platforms in cloud environments. He brings a blend of statistical modelling, ML engineering, and platform development. Data Science & ML Experience: In his current role as a Data Scientist (Sep 2023 – Present), Thomas develops and deploys end-to-end ML models including financial forecasting, customer lifetime value modelling, and price elasticity analysis using sklearn, PyMC, and Prophet. He also architected a full-stack internal analytics and dashboarding platform using Python, Flask, Docker, and GCP, providing leadership with real-time insight beyond traditional BI tools. Previously, as a Data Scientist Intern (Sep 2021 – Sep 2023), Thomas built predictive models used in a commercial product with >80% accuracy, led data-provider integrations, designed scalable prediction pipelines, and worked directly with founders on MVP delivery. He has also delivered large-scale ETL migrations using Prefect and Cloud Run, achieving a 10x reduction in data processing and storage costs, alongside automating processes that saved over 400 hours annually. Alongside his commercial work, he is developing a self-hosted AI assistant using LoRA-fine-tuned LLMs with a custom RAG and TTS pipeline. Tech: Python, SQL, scikit-learn, PyTorch, pandas, polars, PyMC, Prophet, Flask/Django, Prefect, Docker, Git, GCP, AWS, Linux. Thomas is London-based and actively seeking a Data Scientist position. Would you be open to reviewing his CV or having a short introductory chat? Lola Peattie Head hunting the top 1% in AI&ML 🦄",
